# Free basis modulo ± 1 for torsion-free ΓleSL₂(ℤ)

Theorem statement: `Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.exists_generators_free_mod_neg_one_of_forall_trace_ne`
(`3bd3e142-725c-544e-b864-4fd8b4d3ed7e`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `9ce5f5c0-0c4d-5814-b662-464da7d3f2e5`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ (the special linear group of $2\times 2$
integer matrices) of finite index, assume $-1\in\Gamma$, and assume that no $\gamma\in\Gamma$ has
trace $0$, $1$ or $-1$ as an integer matrix. Put $n = 1 + [\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z):\Gamma]/6$,
where the quotient is natural-number division of the index. The assertion is the existence of a
family $g : \mathrm{Fin}\, n \to \Gamma$ with two properties. First, the subgroup of $\Gamma$
generated by the set $\{g_0,\dots,g_{n-1}\}\cup\{-1\}$ (the element $-1$ taken with its membership
in $\Gamma$) is the whole of $\Gamma$. Second, the family has the universal property of a free
generating family with respect to groups in the lowest universe: for every group $L$ in `Type` and
every family $v : \mathrm{Fin}\, n \to L$ there is a group homomorphism $f : \Gamma \to L$ with
$f(g_i) = v_i$ for all $i$. No uniqueness of $f$ is claimed, so the conclusion says that $\Gamma$ is
generated by $n$ elements together with $-1$ and that arbitrary values may be prescribed on those
$n$ elements.

The trace hypothesis rules out elements of finite order other than $\pm 1$, so $\Gamma$ has
torsion-free image $\bar\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb Z)$; the classical statement is that such
a $\bar\Gamma$ is free of rank $1 + [\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z):\Gamma]/6$, and the present form
transports this to $\Gamma$ itself modulo $\pm 1$ in the shape of a generating family on which
homomorphisms may be prescribed freely. It is used in the construction of bases for spaces of
homomorphisms out of $\Gamma$, via
[`ModularCurve.Period.exists_basis_parabolicHoms_castAddHom_comp`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.Period.exists_basis_parabolicHoms_castAddHom_comp).

